      "rationale": "[Literature audit 2026-11-05 (deliverome-analysis PR 236), verdict confirmed_exact: position confirmed at this residue. validation_level surface_and_function -> detected_only (paper reports surface: not_reported, function: not_reported). Paper (PMID 41178115): \"The FLAG tag was inserted between Leu31 and Gln32 in the alpha1 subunit for coimmunoprecipitation experiments, which do not influence trafficking function\". Audit note: Human alpha1 (UniProt P14867-1 cited). FLAG construct used only for co-IP; surface biotinylation and surface staining are not stated to use the FLAG-tagged subunit and the 'do not influence trafficking' claim has no data. Consistent with Yuan 2022 Myc between mature residues 4 and 5 (= 31|32 after the 27-aa signal peptide).] Python confirms residue 31 = L and residue 32 = Q, both within the large extracellular domain (28\u2013251), 4 residues after signal-peptide cleavage and 220 residues from TM1. L1 reports the exact insertion; L2 (independent paper) replicates it and explicitly states no trafficking perturbation, satisfying surface_and_function. The junction is well within the unstructured N-terminal stretch of the mature ectodomain. FLAG tag inserted between Leu31 and Gln32 of full-length GABRA1 in HEK293 cells (QuikChange II mutagenesis); L2 confirms the same construct was used for coimmunoprecipitation and explicitly states it does not influence trafficking function.",
